OL,3,GNEWSAWoman 'blindsided' by early
OL,4,Amenopause
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor many women, going through the
OL,7,Fmenopause is a huge life change and can
OL,8,Fhave wide ranging health implications.
OL,10,FHowever, every year thousands of women
OL,11,Fin the UK are plunged into menopause
OL,12,Fearlier in life due to treatment and
OL,13,Fsurgery.
OL,15,FDanielle Standen, 41, from Banbury, was
OL,16,Fdiagnosed with breast cancer in 2018.
OL,17,FShe said: "As soon as I started my
OL,18,Fchemotherapy treatment, they told me
OL,19,Fthat I would become infertile and I
OL,20,Fwould go into early menopause. That was
OL,21,Fsort of all the information I was
OL,22,Fgiven, so I went into it blindsided."
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
